==============================================================================
verdict
==============================================================================
  The commanded-wrench deadband is NOT the cause. It was the first hypothesis,
  and section 2 refutes it: both force axes are transmitted as nonzero in every
  slot of the hold, and the dead zone the deadband implies is 0.010 m against a
  0.28 m residual.

  The cause is the ESTIMATOR. The loop converges to 0.031 m and 0.9 deg in the
  frame the controller can see; the truth is 0.28 m away because the ESTIMATE
  is 0.28 m away from the truth. There is no absolute position reference after
  the one-shot t0 alignment, so that error is an unbounded random walk.

  It is a property of the simulator, not of smooth_dock_v1: the retained step
  and smooth families sit on the same floor when scored by the same rule. A
  0.15 m TRUE-state tolerance is below that floor, so it would return zero for
  every method under every task, making the endpoint a constant rather than a
  discriminator. pathb2_floor.py quantifies the floor and freezes the
  replacement endpoint.

  wrote results/pathb2_diag.json
